    "updated_at": "2017-01-09T17:08:05Z",
    "body": "Fun.\r\n\r\nWhat Gecko does in this case is use the entry global (the global of the callback function it just compiled) as the incumbent global.  In particular, this means that the \"callback context\" in this case would be the \"settings object\" we pushed in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#getting-the-current-value-of-the-event-handler step 1.9 in Gecko.",
